{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver's reroute was traffic-justified, so this case falls in row (b) of POL-RD-24 rather than row (d), and the driver's conduct is the conduct POL-RD-23 permits. The LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-05004-01 reports HEAVY_TRAFFIC on the Pan-Island Expressway towards Changi between the Clementi Avenue 6 exit and the Clementi Road exit; the recommended route on this trip (EV-TRIP-05004) runs along the PIE to Clementi Road in that direction, so on road, direction and location the advisory intersects the recommended route; and its window 08:15:42-09:27:22 overlaps the trip 08:37:22-08:55:22. The driver's account that the PIE was jammed after Clementi is therefore corroborated by traffic data rather than standing on his assertion alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05004-01", "EV-TRIP-05004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-23", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "evidence[EV-ADVIS-05004-01].payload.overlaps_trip_window",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver does not dispute that he failed to inform the rider of the deviation before or at the point of deviation, so row (a) of POL-RD-24 (informed and agreed, no refund) is not available and the most that can be ordered is the excess distance fare. The chat log EV-CHAT-05004 contains only two messages, both sent before the trip began and neither concerning a reroute, and the trip record EV-TRIP-05004 shows no in-app calls and no messages during the trip (messages_during_trip is empty). The notification obligation in POL-RD-21 is therefore breached and the case is confined to row (b).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05004", "EV-TRIP-05004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-21", "POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.messages_during_trip",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is capped at the excess distance fare of 1.01 SGD, not the 4.00 SGD the rider asks for. The deviation is 1.40 km (actual 9.5 km less recommended 8.1 km, EV-TRIP-05004) and the metered rate is 0.72 SGD per km (EV-FARE-05004); 1.40 x 0.72 = 1.01 SGD without surge, which is the exact figure POL-RD-24 fixes for rows (b) and (d). The rider's asserted figure of 4.00 has no support in the matrix, and the balance of the claim must be refused.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05004", "EV-FARE-05004"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.excess_distance_fare_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
